# Students, Schools, and Enrollment in Science and Humanity Courses in Israeli Secondary Education.

**Authors:** Ayalon, Hanna, Yogev, Abraham

## Abstract
Reports the deteriorating status of the humanities and social sciences versus mathematics in Israeli secondary education that was revealed through a study of 19,047 academic-track students in 201 schools for four years. More able students tended to specialize in mathematics and science, for which student characteristics were the major determinants in course selection. (SLD)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ563453

